        "TextSection": {
            "TextSectionType": "Definition",
            "Contents": "A rare developmental defect during embryogenesis characterized by complete mirror-imaged arrangement of the internal organs across the left-right axis of the body. Primary ciliary dyskinesia Kartagener type is frequently associated. Congenital heart disease are present in 43% of cases which is less frequent than in patients with heterotaxy. Similarly extracardiac and vascular anomalies can be associated (e.g. intestinal malrotation spleen anomalies absence of retrohepatic inferior vena cava bilateral superior vena cava) but less frequently that in heterotaxy."
        },
